# Concept name

AGGREGATE FUNCTIONS

# My understanding

Aggregate functions are SQL functions that combine multiple rows into a single summarized value. They are used to calculate totals, averages, counts, minimums, and maximums from a dataset.

# Why it matters

Aggregate functions are important because they help analyze data quickly. Instead of reviewing every row, we can calculate totals, averages, or statistics that summarize large amounts of information.

# Example

SELECT role, COUNT(*)
FROM employees
GROUP BY role;

This query counts how many employees exist for each role in the company.